<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Kushalgarh State</h1><p class="st-meta">1671 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Kushalgarh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Rathore Rajput chiefship in southern Rajasthan, long a dependency of Banswara with a mostly Bhil population.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kushalgarh was held by a branch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore Rajputs</a> who settled in the hills of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vagad">Vagad</a>. The register dates it to 1671. Its chiefs held their land as feudatories of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banswara-state">Banswara</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Rao ruled a territory of hills and forest with a large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhils">Bhil</a> population, practising subsistence farming. In the British period it was treated as a chiefship under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banswara-state">Banswara</a>, supervised through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputana-agency">Rajputana Agency</a>, rather than as a fully separate salute state.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Kushalgarh joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-state-of-rajasthan">United State of Rajasthan</a> in 1948. It is now a town in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banswara-state">Banswara</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="princely state, 1671 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">princely state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Indian princely states</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.96%;width:5.51%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1671 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-c